ape, located in Belo Horizonte, the capital of Minas Gerais. As one of the largest public universities in Brazil, UFMG has played a significant role in shaping the educational, economic, and cultural fabric of the country, serving a diverse student body and contributing to regional development. Its establishment marked a crucial moment in Brazilian history, reflecting a broader post-colonial shift towards modernity and intellectualism in South America.

